WEBVTT

00:00:00.650 --> 00:00:03.310
North America did not form in one event.

00:00:03.570 --> 00:00:09.010
Its oldest exposed crust includes the roughly four-billion-year-old Acasta Gneiss, while

00:00:09.010 --> 00:00:12.710
much of the Canadian Shield contains younger Precambrian rocks.

00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.430
Successive additions enlarged that core.

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:18.330
A continent's age therefore depends on what you mean:

00:00:18.490 --> 00:00:21.450
the age of a rock, the time a terrane attached, or

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:23.930
the age of sediment covering older basement.

00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.840
Precambrian provinces were added along the southern core, including the Grenville

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.340
region farther southeast. Paleozoic collisions added eastern terranes, and western additions

00:00:34.340 --> 00:00:38.300
continued through later time. Younger sediment covers much older basement across

00:00:38.300 --> 00:00:40.660
the continental platform and coastal plain.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.780
A young color on a surface-geology map does not mean the

00:00:43.780 --> 00:00:45.840
whole crust underneath formed recently.

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:49.560
Southern Florida even conceals a fragment associated with Africa.

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.750
Other continents show the same broad ingredients in different arrangements.

00:00:54.290 --> 00:00:57.890
Western Australia contains an ancient core, with younger additions eastward.

00:00:58.250 --> 00:01:00.550
Africa assembled several Precambrian shields.

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:04.830
Much of Asia joined through Paleozoic and Mesozoic accretion around older

00:01:04.830 --> 00:01:08.890
fragments. India preserves ancient crust carried away during Gondwana's breakup.

00:01:09.310 --> 00:01:12.990
Eastern South America's older regions once connected with Africa, while younger

00:01:12.990 --> 00:01:15.270
construction shaped much of its western side.

00:01:15.920 --> 00:01:21.460
California exposes oceanic crust and sediment, island-arc material, and an accretionary

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:23.820
prism assembled along a convergent margin.

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:28.720
Those imported pieces coexist with rocks formed locally, including Sierra Nevada

00:01:28.720 --> 00:01:30.700
intrusions and later volcanic cover.

00:01:31.060 --> 00:01:34.200
The terrane map specifically omits some units formed in place.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:37.860
Read its purpose and legend before assuming every missing rock is

00:01:37.860 --> 00:01:38.740
absent from the region.

00:01:39.330 --> 00:01:44.230
Continents grow by additions, lose pieces through rifting, shorten internally, stretch,

00:01:44.510 --> 00:01:46.410
and shift along strike-slip faults.

00:01:46.670 --> 00:01:50.610
Deposition can bury that assembly without creating an entirely new continent.

00:01:50.970 --> 00:01:53.850
When reading an age map, ask whether each pattern records basement

00:01:53.850 --> 00:01:56.730
formation, tectonic attachment, or younger cover.

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:00.450
That distinction turns a patchwork of colors into a history you

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:00.930
can explain.
